The AUCROC score is evaluated on out-of-sample predictions, and the MAP@20 is evaluated on category predictions. The final score is the simple average of the two metrics: `12(𝑠𝐴𝑈𝐶+𝑀𝐴𝑃@20)` (line 3, character 0 to line 4, character 0).

The submission format is a csv file with each line representing a single image. The image uuid should be followed by all detected categories and an osd score: `id,categories,osd` (line 4, character 0 to line 5, character 0). The categories should be a space-delimited list of integer codes ordered by the probability the category is present in the image, and the osd field should be a probability or confidence score of whether the image is drawn from a different distribution relative to the training set. 

Note that the categories list will be automatically truncated after 20 entries. 

